---
/*
  Directory of the unstyled test pages.

  Uses the documentation layout rather than TestPageLayout — this page is
  about the fixtures, not one of them, so it should look like the rest of the
  site and keep the sidebar. Everything it links to is raw markup.
*/
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { testPages } from '../../data/testPages';

const checks = [
	'Does it use real Tailwind color names, or did it reach for <code>bg-primary</code>?',
	'Do neutrals sit one rung from their background, and does each button carry the right <code>surface</code> for the card it is in?',
	'Do all five accents stay at 300?',
	'Is the default body size <code>text-sm</code>?',
	'Does the dense inbox get a dense treatment, and the wizard a roomy one?',
	'Do the empty, loading, and error states get the same care as the happy path?',
];
---

<Layout
	title="Test Pages"
	description="Unstyled production markup for testing the design system."
>
	<h1>Test Pages</h1>

	<p>
		Nine pages of real production markup pulled from the <code>voxie</code> app,
		stripped of every Tailwind class and filled with static test data. They
		render as raw semantic HTML. Nothing here is styled — that is the point.
	</p>

	<p>
		They were picked by layout archetype rather than by feature, so the set
		spans what the product actually has to lay out: a dense two-pane inbox, a
		wizard at the opposite density, tables that reflow to cards, a settings
		column, and a page collecting the states everything else falls into.
	</p>

	<h2>The pages</h2>

	<ul class="not-prose space-y-3">
		{
			testPages.map((page) => (
				<li class="leading-snug">
					<a href={page.href} class="text-sky-700 font-semibold hover:text-black">{page.title}</a>
					<br />
					<span class="text-sm">{page.exercises}</span>
					<br />
					<code class="text-xs bg-slate-300/50 px-1 py-0.5 rounded-sm">{page.source}</code>
				</li>
			))
		}
	</ul>

	<h2>Running a trial</h2>

	<p>Point an agent at one page with a brief along these lines:</p>

	<blockquote>
		<p>
			Style this page using the Voxie design system. Read <a
				href="/docs/foundations/color">Color</a
			> and <a href="/docs/foundations/typography">Typography</a> first, and the
			component docs for anything that maps to an existing component. Add
			Tailwind classes to the existing markup. Do not restructure the HTML,
			rename <code>data-test</code> attributes, or change the copy.
		</p>
	</blockquote>

	<p>Then read the result against these:</p>

	<ul>
		{checks.map((check) => <li set:html={check} />)}
	</ul>

	<h2>Resetting</h2>

	<p>
		These are fixtures, so they have to survive being styled. Note the commit
		before handing a page over; <code>git checkout -- src/pages/test-pages/</code
		> puts every page back to raw markup.
	</p>

	<p>
		The same brief, plus notes on how the markup was stripped, lives in <code
			>src/pages/test-pages/_README.md</code
		>.
	</p>
</Layout>
